quran[21]{c,v,t}:
  100,10,"and whatever is in the breasts is made apparent,"
  100,11,"indeed, their Lord shall be All-Aware of them that Day."
  101,1,The Terrible Calamity!
  101,2,What is the Terrible Calamity?
  101,3,What will make you realise what the Terrible Calamity is?
  101,4,"(It is) the Day when people will be like scattered moths,"
  101,5,and the mountains will be like carded wool.
  101,6,"As for him whose scales (of good deeds) are heavy,"
  101,7,he shall have a pleasant life.
  101,8,"But as for him whose scales (of good deeds) are light,"
  101,9,his home shall be the abyss.
  101,10,What will make you realise what it is?
  101,11,"It is a (deep, bottomless pit of) Blazing Fire."
  102,1,"The competition of wealth accumulation distracts you (from God),"
  102,2,until you visit the graves.
  102,3,"No, indeed! Soon you will come to know!"
  102,4,"Again, no, indeed! Soon you will come to know!"
  102,5,"No, indeed! If only you had known (the consequence of greed) with certain knowledge (you would have acted differently)."
  102,6,You will most definitely see the Hellfire.
  102,7,"Again, you will most surely see it with the eye of certainty."
  102,8,"Then, surely you will be questioned that Day, about the blessings (bestowed upon you in the world)."
